{
  "id": "kl-001",
  "description": "(0.5.0) Keyless-signing known answers (RFC-ACDP-0021), executed by scripts/conformance-runner.py. Vector 1 is a golden acdp:key-attestation body minted by the registry: JCS canonical form, content_hash and the registry's Ed25519 signature over the ASCII content_hash, plus the §5.3 metadata rules (fingerprint, JWK thumbprint, key_id fragment, window bound). Vector 2 is a keyless-signed body that references it: content_hash and the ephemeral key's signature. Vector 3 is the §5.1 proof of possession and token hash. Vector 4 is the §8 key-status table and vector 5 the §7 supersession table; vector 6 (added in 0.5.0-draft.2) is a verify-only ecdsa-p256 proof of possession under p256_test_keypair: the 64-byte r||s form verifies and the same signature DER-encoded is rejected (§5.1); the runner replays both algorithms. Test keypairs MUST NOT be used in production.",
  "tags": [
    "keyless",
    "registry",
    "consumer",
    "0.5.0",
    "known-answer",
    "golden"
  ],
  "applies_to_profiles": [
    "acdp-registry-keyless",
    "acdp-consumer-keyless"
  ],
