  "notes": "The token is a placeholder string, not a JWT: kl-001 pins only token_hash. Token verification itself (issuer keys, aud, exp, cnf.jkt) follows AITP RFC-AITP-0002 §2 and is exercised behaviorally by kl-002. Timestamps are canonical, so the runner compares them as strings. Cross-implementation known answer (2026-10-31): acdp-rs 0.19.0 and acdp-verifier-py 0195978 reproduce every vector byte for byte at spec da386c4. The consumer-side values (vectors 1, 2 and 4) back RFC-ACDP-0021's Final consumer side. Vectors 3, 5 and 6 are frozen too, though the registry sections they exercise stay Draft.",
